body:
Found it before you even run anything: the exporter doesn't filter by person — it grabs every message in the window. I searched the raw CSVs for her verbatim Sep 7 lines ("why people go to therapy," "actually mental," "PROMPT INJECTING") and got zero hits. Her words never landed in the Mac's database at all. It's a sync problem, not an extraction problem.

Paste this on your Mac — it shows every handle that could be hers, how stale the Mac's database is, and every inbound sender in the Aug 19–Sep 8 window:

```bash
DB=~/Library/Messages/chat.db; T=/tmp/chatdiag.db; cp "$DB" "$T" 2>/dev/null; cp "$DB-wal" "$T-wal" 2>/dev/null; cp "$DB-shm" "$T-shm" 2>/dev/null; sqlite3 "$T" "
SELECT '--- handles matching ally/lubin ---';
SELECT ROWID, id, service FROM handle WHERE id LIKE '%lubin%' OR id LIKE '%ally%';
SELECT '--- chats matching ally/lubin ---';
SELECT ROWID, chat_identifier, display_name FROM chat WHERE chat_identifier LIKE '%lubin%' OR chat_identifier LIKE '%ally%';
SELECT '--- newest 3 messages in db (mac staleness check) ---';
SELECT datetime(date/1000000000 + 978307200,'unixepoch') FROM message ORDER BY date DESC LIMIT 3;
SELECT '--- inbound senders Aug 19 - Sep 8 ---';
SELECT COALESCE(h.id,'(no handle)'), COUNT(*) FROM message m LEFT JOIN handle h ON h.ROWID=m.handle_id WHERE m.is_from_me=0 AND m.date >= (strftime('%s','2026-08-19')-978307200)*1000000000 AND m.date < (strftime('%s','2026-09-09')-978307200)*1000000000 GROUP BY h.id ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 25;
"; rm -f /tmp/chatdiag.db*
```

Needs Full Disk Access for Terminal if it errors on the copy. Send me what it prints and I'll read it.
